          deckDescription: 'Twenty-nine cards total: seven ranks (ace, king, queen, jack, ten, nine, six) in each of four French suits, plus one joker. The joker serves as the middle trump in this pitch variant; twos, threes, fours, fives, sevens, and eights are removed.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Each suit has seven cards in this stripped pack. Trump is determined by the bid; the joker is the middle trump (between jack and ten of trump). Follow suit when able.',
          rankDescription: 'Seven ranks per suit used in play: ace, king, queen, jack, ten, nine, six (twos through fives and eights removed). One joker counts as the middle trump. Standard pitch ranking with the joker as a permanent trump card.',
